Naming
------
"Tlilli", "Tlapalli" and "amoxtli" are Nahuatl words: tlilli is black ink,
tlapalli is red ink, and amoxtli is a book or codex. In the codex tradition the
paired phrase "in tlilli in tlapalli", the black ink and the red ink, stood for
writing and the knowledge it carried. The project uses these three words, and
no others from the language, to name the author's text, the agent's proposals
and a manuscript. It claims no rights in the Nahuatl language or in the words
themselves; section 6 of the Apache License grants no trademark rights in the
project name either.
